  "notes": "### macOS Universal 2.3.6\n\nFor Intel and Apple silicon Macs running macOS 14.4 or later.\n\n- Open the renamed **Reference** panel, adjust pen width in a compact field, and use the toolbar arrows to switch between open documents.\n- Scroll continuously through PDFs with the mouse wheel, trackpad, or scrollbar. Pages render as they come into view.\n- Add text, pen strokes, and highlights. Use Command-Z and Shift-Command-Z or the Edit menu to undo and redo completed edits in the active reference. Annotations stay on their pages when you reopen a document.\n\nBuilt and tested on an Intel Mac Pro. The app is signed ad hoc. Every bundled Mach-O file contains x86_64 and arm64 slices. The arm64 slices were verified structurally.\n\nSource commit: `20576ac17d84c4b78f248f7b8dd026b86c9d83b3`. The corresponding source archive, third-party notices and source references, and SHA-256 checksums accompany the DMG.\n",
